{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"953db6c3-7c8f-4792-afbc-ff1678c3ca90","step":{"id":"s1","script":"For a launch and landing at the same height, range depends on the launch angle.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Projectile range versus angle"},{"op":"equation","id":"rangeformula","region":"left","latex":"R=\\frac{v_0^2\\sin(2\\theta)}{g}"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"953db6c3-7c8f-4792-afbc-ff1678c3ca90","step":{"id":"s2","script":"With launch speed fixed, the sine factor controls how far the projectile travels.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"factor","anchor":{"el":"rangeformula","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"v₀ and g fixed; maximize sin(2θ)"},{"op":"axes","id":"rangeaxes","region":"right","x":{"min":0,"max":1.5708,"label":"θ"},"y":{"min":0,"max":1.1,"label":"R g / v₀²"}}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"953db6c3-7c8f-4792-afbc-ff1678c3ca90","step":{"id":"s3","script":"The normalized range rises, peaks at forty-five degrees, then falls symmetrically.","ops":[{"op":"curve","id":"rangecurve","axes_id":"rangeaxes","expr":"sin(2*x)","domain":[0,1.5708]},{"op":"text","id":"peak","anchor":{"el":"rangeaxes","side":"below","gap":0.06},"content":"maximum at θ = 45°"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Which launch angle gives the greatest range on level ground?","expected_gist":"45 degrees"}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"953db6c3-7c8f-4792-afbc-ff1678c3ca90","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Thus complementary angles have equal range, but forty-five degrees gives the maximum.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"conclusion","anchor":{"el":"rangeformula","side":"below","gap":0.18},"latex":"R_{\\max}=\\frac{v_0^2}{g}\\quad\\text{at}\\quad\\theta=45^\\circ"},{"op":"text","id":"symmetry","anchor":{"el":"peak","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"θ and 90° − θ give equal ranges"}],"checkpoint":null}}
